  "text101": "Our little crew is building a new home. And today, you get to help.",
  "text102": "There's our landing pad. Next stop: your first footsteps on Mars!",
  "text103": "Touchdown! Take a look around. I think you are going to like it here.",
  "text104": "I'm Dhrubo, your robot buddy. Stick with me. We make a pretty good team.",
  "text105": "Come on, Kitty! Follow me to the solar panels.",
  "text106": "A little dust is blocking our sunshine. Give both panels a good brush.",
  "text107": "Look at that shine! One more panel to go.",
  "text108": "Beautiful! Now let us connect the panels to our base.",
  "text109": "Take the cable from the solar panels and plug it into the habitat.",
  "text110": "The lights are on! You just powered our new home.",
  "text111": "Kitty, a solar storm warning. We need to get the crew into our shelter.",
  "text112": "Leave the tools here. Follow the path back to the airlock with me.",
  "text113": "We are both inside. Close the outer door first.",
  "text114": "Outer door closed. Now fill the airlock with air.",
  "text115": "Nice and steady. We wait until the air pressure is ready.",
  "text116": "Pressure ready. You can open the inner door now.",
  "text117": "Our crewmate is waiting. Bring everyone into the shielded room.",
  "text118": "We are sheltered. Connect our backup battery to the air system and the radio.",
  "text119": "That uses the whole battery. Let us keep the air and radio powered first.",
  "text120": "Air is flowing. Radio is working. Our crew is in good hands.",
  "text121": "We stay in the shelter while the radiation is elevated. Let us check the monitor.",
  "text122": "Still elevated outside. We will stay right here together.",
  "text123": "The readings are falling. We still need to wait for the all-clear.",
  "text124": "Our base has confirmed the all-clear! Let us check our equipment with the rover.",
  "text125": "You are driving from inside the base. Visit each marker and scan the equipment.",
  "text126": "Good scan! Drive to the next glowing marker.",
  "text127": "A little rock in our way. Try steering around it.",
  "text128": "Every system checked. Everyone safe. That is what a great astronaut does.",
  "text129": "Mission complete, Cadet Kitty! Welcome to the crew.",
  "text130": "A new world",
  "text131": "First footsteps",
  "text132": "Hello, Mars",
  "text133": "A little sunshine",
  "text134": "Power our home",
  "text135": "Together, back to base",
  "text136": "One door at a time",
  "text137": "A safe place",
  "text138": "Look after the crew",
  "text139": "A little patience",
  "text140": "Ready to explore again",
  "text141": "Small paws. Big adventure.",
  "text142": "Welcome to the crew",
  "text143": "Sunshine helper",
  "text144": "Crew keeper",
  "text145": "Storm smart",
  "text146": "Rover ranger",
  "text147": "Solar array",
  "text148": "Radio mast",
  "text149": "Landing pad",
  "text150": "Follow Dhrubo",
  "text151": "Brush the panel",
  "text152": "Airlock",
  "text153": "Crew shelter",
  "text154": "Solar sweep",
  "text155": "A little dust. A big difference.",
  "text156": "~ 1 min",
  "text157": "Maintenance",
  "text158": "Dust is dimming our solar array. Head outside and bring the outpost back to full power.",
  "text159": "Clean all three solar panels",
  "text160": "Keep some time on the clock",
  "text161": "Move with arrows / WASD. Hold Space near a panel to clean. Or tap a panel to walk over and clean it.",
  "text162": "Dust reduces the sunlight reaching solar cells. Cleaning restores output in this simplified training scenario. Real Mars missions cannot count on an astronaut or a cleaning wind.",
  "text163": "Cargo across the crater",
  "text164": "Precious cargo. Rocky road.",
  "text165": "~ 2 min",
  "text166": "Navigation",
  "text167": "The supply drop landed beyond the ridge. Pilot your rover, collect three crates and bring them home.",
  "text168": "Collect all three supply crates",
  "text169": "Return to the landing pad",
  "text170": "Drive with arrows / WASD, or tap a destination. Steer around rocks. Collected crates load automatically; return to the glowing pad.",
  "text171": "Surface missions need route planning and safe delivery. Our rover has forgiving game handling; its fuel use, collisions and terrain are invented training rules.",
  "text172": "Keep the lights on",
  "text173": "One battery. Many possibilities.",
  "text174": "~ 3 min",
  "text175": "Resource planning",
  "text176": "Three shifts. Less sunlight each time. Allocate power to keep air reserves healthy and care for a pre-grown crop tray.",
  "text177": "Finish with air reserves ≥ 45",
  "text178": "Grow the crop tray to ≥ 60%",
  "text179": "Move the power sliders, then run a shift. Two units are reserved for essential systems. Unspent units stay unused; optional rover charging earns bonus points.",
  "text180": "Life support needs oxygen production as well as carbon-dioxide removal. Essential air cleaning and thermal control stay powered here. Crop growth is accelerated; this tray is already partly grown and adds fresh food, not a complete diet.",
  "text181": "Beat the solar storm",
  "text182": "Good explorers know when to return.",
  "text183": "Safety & timing",
  "text184": "Practise a short sensor route before a training alert. Once the alert starts, leave equipment behind and head for shelter.",
  "text185": "Sensors are optional practice",
  "text186": "Reach shelter when the alert starts",
  "text187": "Move with arrows / WASD, or tap a destination. Walk over both sensors, then return to the glowing shelter. Exposure starts rising after 12 seconds.",
  "text188": "Solar energetic particles can increase radiation at Mars. Prepared shelter can reduce exposure. The countdown and exposure index here are fictional game rules, not NASA radiation readings or health limits. Shielding stays protective without consuming power.",
  "text189": "Unknown mission",
  "text190": "Plan your first shift. A crop allocation of 3 adds 30% growth.",
  "text191": "Too much power requested. Lower a slider before running this shift.",
  "text192": [
    "Shift ",
    ": air ",
    "",
    ", crops +",
    "%. ",
    ""
  ],
  "text193": "Sunlight is fading; adjust your next allocation.",
  "text194": [
    "Shift ",
    " complete · air ",
    " · crops ",
    "%"
  ],
  "text195": "A chance to re-plan",
  "text196": "Air reserves became too low. Try giving the air processor at least 3 units each shift.",
  "text197": "Habitat, happy. Crew, happier.",
  "text198": "Your outpost needs a new plan",
  "text199": "You kept air in reserve and cared for a crop tray while sunlight faded. Extra rover power earned bonus points.",
  "text200": "Keep air at 45 or above and get crops to 60%. Try air 3 and crops 3 for the first two shifts, then protect air on the third.",
  "text201": "Panel restored · array output increased",
  "text202": "A brighter day on Mars",
  "text203": "All three panels are clear. You restored sunlight access and brought the training array back online.",
  "text204": "Rock contact · −12 rover integrity",
  "text205": [
    "Supply crate secured · ",
    "/3"
  ],
  "text206": "Special delivery: successful",
  "text207": "Your supplies are safely home. Careful steering protected both the rover and its cargo.",
  "text208": "Let’s choose another route",
  "text209": "Your training rover needs a reset. Give rocks a little more space and try a smoother path.",
  "text210": [
    "Field sensor recovered · ",
    "/2"
  ],
  "text211": "Safe paws. Mission accomplished.",
  "text212": "You reached shelter. Sensors are optional once the alert begins: people come first. Ending an outdoor task early can be the smartest mission decision.",
  "text213": "Training paused. Try a new route.",
  "text214": "Head straight to each panel and keep the cleaning tool active until it reaches 100%.",
  "text215": "Visit both sensors, then head straight back to the shelter at the upper left.",
  "text216": "Collect all three crates and return to the glowing pad in the lower left.",
  "text217": "Cadet Kitty",
